## Why This Is Asked
This prompts designing scalable, isolated analytics pipelines with per-tenant data lakes and strong governance.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation across storage and compute
- Exactly-once ingestion with idempotency
- OpenTelemetry data normalization
- Per-tenant data marts in Athena
- Data masking and RBAC
- Lifecycle and cost controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js Lambda dedup skeleton
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const {tenant_id, message_id, payload} = JSON.parse(event.body || '{}');
  const key = {TenantId: tenant_id, MessageId: message_id};
  await ddb.put({TableName:'Idempotency', Item: key, ConditionExpression:'attribute_not_exists(MessageId)'}).promise();
  // forward to S3 after normalization
  return {statusCode: 200, body: 'ok'};
}
```

